1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,522
Two bakers opened their shops

2
00:00:02,522 --> 00:00:03,900
on the same street.

3
00:00:04,150 --> 00:00:05,721
Both started with exactly

4
00:00:05,721 --> 00:00:06,900
six hundred dollars.

5
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,250
Both spent their

6
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,300
money making bread.

7
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:10,825
And by the end

8
00:00:10,825 --> 00:00:12,050
of the day, both

9
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:13,275
had sold one thousand

10
00:00:13,275 --> 00:00:14,500
dollars' worth of bread.

11
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:16,886
But the next morning,

12
00:00:16,886 --> 00:00:18,000
something strange happened.

13
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:19,664
One baker opened his

14
00:00:19,664 --> 00:00:20,650
shop like usual.

15
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,550
The other couldn't even

16
00:00:22,550 --> 00:00:24,100
afford to buy flour.

17
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:25,600
Here's what happened.

18
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,389
The first baker sold his

19
00:00:28,389 --> 00:00:29,900
bread directly to customers.

20
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:32,100
Every customer paid him immediately.

21
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,079
So by the end of

22
00:00:34,079 --> 00:00:35,757
the day, he had one

23
00:00:35,757 --> 00:00:37,100
thousand dollars in cash.

24
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,350
He used six hundred dollars

25
00:00:39,350 --> 00:00:41,200
to prepare the next batch.

26
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:44,100
And the business kept running.

27
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:46,671
But the second baker

28
00:00:46,671 --> 00:00:47,700
did something different.

29
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,654
Instead of selling to customers,

30
00:00:49,654 --> 00:00:51,308
he sold all his bread

31
00:00:51,308 --> 00:00:52,300
to a supermarket.

32
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:54,544
The supermarket agreed to pay

33
00:00:54,544 --> 00:00:56,100
him one thousand dollars...

34
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:58,600
Sixty days later.

35
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:00,550
Now think about that.

36
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:01,825
Both bakers made

37
00:01:01,825 --> 00:01:02,850
the same sales.

38
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:04,536
Both had four hundred

39
00:01:04,536 --> 00:01:05,973
dollars in gross profit,

40
00:01:05,973 --> 00:01:07,050
before other expenses.

41
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:08,500
But one had a

42
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:09,700
thousand dollars in cash.

43
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,389
And the other had a

44
00:01:11,389 --> 00:01:12,500
thousand dollars on paper.

45
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:14,056
He had to wait sixty

46
00:01:14,056 --> 00:01:15,100
days to collect it.

47
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:16,250
And without additional cash,

48
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:17,250
he couldn't afford to

49
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:18,000
make another batch.

50
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:20,200
You see, making a

51
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:21,700
profit and having cash

52
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:23,200
are two different things.

53
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:25,314
Because a business can look

54
00:01:25,314 --> 00:01:27,029
profitable on paper... and still

55
00:01:27,029 --> 00:01:28,400
run out of money.
